    {
      "page_title": "Authentication: JWT and OAuth 2.0",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Q11. What is the difference between authentication and authorization?",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "==Authentication== proves **who** you are. ==Authorization== decides **what** you may do. Authn always runs first."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Authn: password, MFA, token, or certificate",
            "Authz: roles, scopes, policies, ownership checks",
            "Failed authn gives 401, failed authz gives 403",
            "Page 2 covers the 401 vs 403 split"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Q12. How does a JWT work and what are its three parts?",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A ==JWT== is a signed `header.payload.signature` string. The API checks the signature and needs **no** database lookup."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Header names the algorithm, e.g. `RS256`",
            "Payload holds claims: `sub`, `exp`, `aud`, `scope`",
            "Signature covers header + payload, so edits are caught",
            "Payload is only base64url, **not** encrypted"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "token = h.p.s  (base64url parts)",
            "h = {\"alg\":\"RS256\"}",
            "p = {\"sub\":\"42\",\"exp\":1790000000}",
            "s = sign(h + \".\" + p, key)"
          ],
          "note": "payload is readable, never secret"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Q13. What is the difference between access tokens and refresh tokens?",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "An ==access token== is a short-lived key sent to the API. A ==refresh token== is long-lived and only mints new access tokens."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Access: 5-15 minutes, sent on every API call",
            "Refresh: days or weeks, sent only to the auth server",
            "Short access life limits damage if it leaks",
            "Rotate refresh tokens and revoke them on logout"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Q14. How does the OAuth 2.0 Authorization Code flow with PKCE work?",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The app sends a hashed secret (==code_challenge==) with the login request. It later redeems the one-time code by proving the original `code_verifier`."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "App makes a random `code_verifier`",
            "`code_challenge` = BASE64URL(SHA256(verifier))",
            "User logs in, redirect returns a one-time `code`",
            "App POSTs `code` + verifier and gets tokens",
            "A stolen code is useless without the verifier"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "App",
                "sub": "challenge",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "Login",
                "sub": "consent",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "Redirect",
                "sub": "code",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "Token call",
                "sub": "code + verifier",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Q15. What is the difference between session-based and token-based authentication?",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "==Sessions== keep state on the server and send an opaque ID cookie. ==Tokens== carry signed state, so the server stays stateless."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cookies are sent automatically, so guard against CSRF",
            "Tokens in `localStorage` are exposed to XSS",
            "Pick sessions for one web app, tokens for many APIs"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Interview tip",
          "text": "Say the trade-off: JWTs scale easily, but revoking one is hard."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "cognito",
      "subtitle": "Q11 to Q15"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Token Storage, Validation and Rotation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Aspect",
            "Session",
            "Token (JWT)"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "State",
              "Server store",
              "In the token"
            ],
            [
              "Revoke",
              "Instant",
              "Wait for exp"
            ],
            [
              "Scaling",
              "Shared Redis",
              "Stateless"
            ],
            [
              "Sent as",
              "Cookie",
              "Bearer header"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Safer token storage",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`HttpOnly` + `Secure` cookie hides the token from JS",
            "Add `SameSite=Lax` or `Strict` to blunt CSRF",
            "Keep access tokens in memory, not `localStorage`",
            "Revoke by session ID, or keep a short denylist"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Validating a JWT",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Verify the signature with a pinned algorithm",
            "Reject expired tokens: check `exp` and `nbf`",
            "Check `iss` and `aud` match your API",
            "Never accept `alg: none` from a client"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "jwt.verify(token, pubKey, {",
            "  algorithms: [\"RS256\"],",
            "  audience: \"api.app.io\",",
            "  issuer: \"https://auth.app.io\"",
            "});"
          ],
          "note": "pin the algorithm, check aud and iss"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Refresh token rotation",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "Access expires",
                "sub": "401 from API",
                "ink": "red"
              },
              {
                "text": "POST refresh",
                "sub": "to auth server",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "New pair",
                "sub": "access + refresh",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "Old refresh",
                "sub": "revoked",
                "ink": "orange"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Each refresh token works exactly once",
            "Reuse of an old one signals theft",
            "Then revoke the whole token family",
            "User must log in again"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Authn vs authz in layers",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Check",
            "Question",
            "Fails with"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Token valid",
              "who are you?",
              "401"
            ],
            [
              "Scope",
              "may this app act?",
              "403"
            ],
            [
              "Role",
              "may this user act?",
              "403"
            ],
            [
              "Ownership",
              "is it yours?",
              "403 / 404"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Remember",
          "text": "A valid token proves identity only. Check ownership on every object."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Common auth mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Putting secrets or PII in the JWT payload",
            "Access tokens that live for days",
            "No `exp` claim, so tokens never die",
            "Skipping `aud` check across microservices"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Interview tip",
          "text": "Name PKCE for mobile and SPA apps. Implicit flow is deprecated."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "cognito",
      "subtitle": "Q11 to Q15"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "CORS and API Security",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Q16. What is CORS and why does the browser block cross-origin requests?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "CORS lets a server say which other ==origins== may read its responses. The browser enforces the **same-origin policy** and hides the reply unless the server opts in.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Origin = scheme + host + port",
            "Blocking happens in the browser, not the server",
            "curl and Postman ignore CORS entirely",
            "Opt in with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Page origin",
            "API origin",
            "Allowed?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "app.io",
              "app.io/api",
              "same origin"
            ],
            [
              "app.io",
              "api.app.io",
              "cross: needs CORS"
            ],
            [
              "http://app.io",
              "https://app.io",
              "cross: scheme"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Q17. What is a CORS preflight and when does it fire?",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A preflight is an automatic ==OPTIONS== request the browser sends first to ask permission for a non-simple request.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Triggers: PUT, PATCH, DELETE methods",
            "Triggers: custom headers or `application/json`",
            "Triggers: credentials with a custom header",
            "Cache the answer with `Access-Control-Max-Age`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "OPTIONS",
                "sub": "preflight"
              },
              {
                "text": "204 + Allow-*",
                "sub": "server agrees"
              },
              {
                "text": "Real request",
                "sub": "PUT /orders"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Q18. How do you defend against the OWASP API Top 10?",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Enforce authorization on every object and function, never trust the client. The top risk, ==BOLA==, is changing an ID to read someone else's data.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const o = await db.order(id);",
            "if (o.userId !== req.user.id)",
            "  return res.sendStatus(403);",
            "// check owner on EVERY object"
          ],
          "note": "Never trust the ID in the URL"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Per-object ownership check, not just login",
            "Rate limit and cap response sizes",
            "Allow-list fields to stop mass assignment",
            "Keep an inventory of old API versions"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Q19. API keys vs OAuth vs mTLS?",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Method",
            "Identifies",
            "Best for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "API key",
              "the app",
              "server-to-server, quotas"
            ],
            [
              "OAuth 2.0",
              "user + scopes",
              "third-party delegated access"
            ],
            [
              "mTLS",
              "both machines",
              "internal zero-trust"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Keys are static secrets: rotate, never ship in browser code",
            "OAuth tokens are short-lived and scoped (see page 3)",
            "mTLS: both sides present certificates"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Remember",
          "text": "Bearer tokens in headers are immune to CSRF. Cookie auth is not."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "waf",
      "subtitle": "Q16 to Q20"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Injection, XSS and CSRF Defences",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Q20. How do you stop SQL injection, XSS and CSRF?",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Attack",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "SQL injection",
              "parameterized queries"
            ],
            [
              "XSS",
              "output encoding + CSP"
            ],
            [
              "CSRF",
              "SameSite cookies + token"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// BAD: string concatenation",
            "db.query(\"... id=\" + id);",
            "// GOOD: bound parameter",
            "db.query(\"... id=$1\", [id]);"
          ],
          "note": "Never concatenate user input"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "SQL injection defences",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Bind every value as a query parameter",
            "ORMs are safe only if you avoid raw strings",
            "Allow-list column names used in `ORDER BY`",
            "Give the DB user least privilege, no DROP"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "XSS: where it bites an API",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "Payload lives in",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Stored",
              "database field",
              "encode on output"
            ],
            [
              "Reflected",
              "URL or query",
              "encode + validate"
            ],
            [
              "DOM-based",
              "client JS",
              "avoid `innerHTML`"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "CSRF defence steps",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Set `SameSite=Lax` or `Strict` on cookies",
            "Send a random CSRF token in a header",
            "Check the `Origin` header on writes",
            "Never change state on a `GET` request"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Useful security headers",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'",
            "X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff",
            "Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000"
          ],
          "note": "set on every API response"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Interview tip",
          "text": "Name the layers: validate input, encode output, use least privilege."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Remember",
          "text": "JSON APIs still need `Content-Type` checks. Reject unexpected types with 415."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "waf",
